.TH "OSTRYA\-RECEIVE" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-receive \- Receive one push session over standard input and standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya receive [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receive one push session over standard input and standard output.
.PP
By default, \fB\%ostrya push\fR runs this command on the server over ssh. The receive policy comes from the repository config, or from the file of \%\-\-policy. Standard output carries the frames of the session alone. For each warning of the session, the command writes one \fB\%warning: STEP: MESSAGE\fR line to standard error. It writes nothing else, also under \%\-\-verbose. The exit status is \%0 after a committed session, also with warnings, and \%1 otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fIFILE\fR
Read the receive policy from FILE in place of the repository config.
.IP
FILE holds the receive, trust, and key groups and the remote sections, in the \%key\-file format of the config. The command then ignores these groups and sections in the repository config. \fB\%[core] auto\-update\-summary\fR and \fB\%[ex\-ostrya] detached\-metadata\-exclude\fR still come from the repository config. FILE must be a regular \%UTF\-8 file of \%1 MiB or less.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
